// The Anchor board: Renode's STM32F746 model plus the Discovery's green LED.
//
// Things worth knowing about this model:
//   - `flash` is plain memory, 2 MiB at 0x08000000. Renode does not model
//     the STM32F7 flash controller, so there is no erase/program sequence
//     and an erased byte reads 0x00, not 0xFF as on the real chip.
//   - `usart1` is the console (src/board/console.adb).
//   - The file this one builds on downloads a register description (SVD)
//     the first time it is used, so the very first run needs the network.

using "platforms/cpus/stm32f746.repl"

UserLED: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpioPortI

gpioPortI:
    1 -> UserLED@0
